      probabilityWeightedOutlook: "We assign a 50% probability to a cautiously bullish scenario, driven by sustained institutional demand and regulatory clarity. A 30% probability is given to a neutral, range-bound market, influenced by conflicting signals. A 20% probability is assigned to a bearish downturn, primarily due to broader market contagion or significant regulatory setbacks.",
