      neutralCase: "A neutral perspective suggests that the crypto market will continue its trajectory of growth alongside significant challenges. Institutional adoption will progress, but at a measured pace, while regulatory clarity will remain elusive in many regions, leading to ongoing legal battles. Security incidents will persist, necessitating continuous improvements in platform safeguards and user education, resulting in a market that matures incrementally but remains volatile and risky.",
      probabilityWeightedOutlook: "Our probability-weighted outlook assigns a 45% chance to a \'bullish yet cautious\' scenario, where institutional adoption continues to drive growth but is tempered by regulatory headwinds and security concerns. A 35% chance is given to a \'volatile but resilient\' scenario, where the market absorbs regulatory and security shocks, finding new equilibrium. A 20% chance is assigned to a \'challenging and restrictive\' scenario, where punitive regulations and widespread scams significantly hinder growth and adoption.",
      potentialCatalysts: ["Further spot Bitcoin ETF approvals globally, particularly in major financial centers.", "Resolution of key regulatory lawsuits, providing clearer legal precedents.", "Major tech companies implementing stricter security protocols and liability frameworks for crypto apps.", "Increased adoption of Bitcoin by sovereign wealth funds or additional public companies.", "Significant technological advancements improving crypto security and user experience."],
