    quickAnswer: "Surging U.S. government debt yields are leading to foreign institutional investor (FII) outflows from Indian equities and debt, contributing to Indian Rupee depreciation and escalating borrowing costs for Indian businesses and the government, thereby impacting overall market liquidity and investor sentiment.",
