      neutralCase: "Markets continue to exhibit range-bound behavior as investors weigh persistent inflation risks against pockets of economic resilience. Central banks maintain a data-dependent, cautious approach, leading to gradual policy adjustments. Sectoral performance remains divergent, with energy and defensive stocks showing strength while growth-sensitive sectors face headwinds. No clear path to either a strong recovery or a deep recession materializes.",
      probabilityWeightedOutlook: "A probability-weighted outlook suggests a \'cautious stability\' scenario, where markets remain volatile but generally avoid a severe downturn, largely due to the offsetting forces of sector-specific strengths (like energy) against macroeconomic headwinds (like inflation and housing pressure). There\'s a 45% chance of a neutral outcome, 30% for a bearish scenario, and 25% for a bullish one, reflecting the current balanced but fragile economic landscape.",
      potentialCatalysts: ["Lower-than-expected UK CPI data easing BOE pressure.", "Significant easing of global energy prices.", "Stronger-than-anticipated corporate earnings reports.", "Clear signals of a \'soft landing\' from major central banks.", "Resolution of geopolitical tensions impacting commodity markets."],
